==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|dauðr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*daudaz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈtøyːðʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|øyːðʏr|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|dauðari|dauðastur}}

# [[dead]]
#: {{syn|is|andvana|dáinn|látinn}}

====Usage notes====
* '''''Dauður''''' can sound heartless in modern Icelandic when used for someone the speaker, or the people they are speaking to, knew. When referring to a specific person, use {{m|is|dáinn}} or {{m|is|látinn}} instead, unless you are talking about a historical figure or someone otherwise unconnected to you.

====Inflection====
{{is-decl-adj-1|d|au|ð}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|dauður sjór}} ([[sea]] where no fish is caught)
* {{l|is|fyrr skal ég dauður liggja}} (over my dead body)
* {{l|is|nýdauður}}
* {{l|is|steindauður}}
* {{l|is|víndauður}} (passed out from drinking)

